  "era": "judges",
  "lifespan": "c. 1150–1050 BC",
  "summary": "Boaz was a wealthy landowner in Bethlehem and a relative of Naomi's deceased husband. He showed great kindness to the Moabite Ruth when she gleaned grain in his fields. As a kinsman-redeemer, he took Ruth as his wife and became the grandfather of King David—and thus part of the lineage of the Messiah.",
